### 🟢 Regular Chat Memory Example
# Sends a user message to the regular chat memory controller
GET http://localhost:8080/memory?message=Hello AI
Accept: application/json

### 🟢 Test Different Queries
# Experiment with different prompts
GET http://localhost:8080/memory?message=Give me a quick tip on Spring AI
Accept: application/json

### 🟢 Another Example
# Try a follow-up message
GET http://localhost:8080/memory?message=Can you summarize our conversation so far?
Accept: application/json


### 🟢 Compacting Chat Memory - Basic Chat
# Sends a user message to the compacting chat memory controller.
# Automatic compaction will occur when message count reaches the configured threshold.
GET http://localhost:8080/compact/memory?message=Hello AI
Accept: application/json

### 🟢 Compacting Chat Memory - Follow-up Message
# Adds a follow-up message to the conversation.
# Observe how context is preserved while old messages are summarized once threshold is reached.
GET http://localhost:8080/compact/memory?message=Continue the previous discussion with context preserved
Accept: application/json

### 🟢 Compacting Chat Memory - Manual Compaction
# Trigger compaction manually to summarize oldest messages regardless of threshold.
# Returns details about the compaction (messages and tokens before/after).
GET http://localhost:8080/compact/trigger
Accept: application/json

### 🟢 Compacting Chat Memory - Clear Memory
# Completely clears the conversation history for a fresh start.
# Useful for testing or starting a new session.
GET http://localhost:8080/compact/clear
Accept: application/json